    "labelChirho": "Shubael / Shebuel (proper name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "A Hebrew proper name (שׁוּבָאֵל) with variant spelling Shebuel, referring to Levitical descendants: (1) a son of Gershom son of Moses who was chief officer over the treasuries (1 Chr 23:16; 26:24), and (2) a son of Heman the musician (1 Chr 25:4, 20). The two clusters differ only in transliteration convention (Shubael vs. Shebuel) and the presence/absence of the conjunction waw, not in semantic content. Evidence: eng 'Shuvael/Shevuel,' spa 'Shubael/Sebuel,' arb 'شُوبَائِيلُ/شَبُوئِيلُ,' hin 'शबूएल,' kor '쉐부엘,' swa 'Shubaeli/Shebueli.' All render the same proper noun.",
    "senseIdsChirho": [137659, 137660]
  }
